n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{40}}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{40}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{40}}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{40}}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U,$ $Σ,$ and $V:$ \n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{40} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{40}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186434257 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3868de93-336f-5be1-b8c0-ee5d1d36c94c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434257 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186371388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434258 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186434260 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434258 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ad6e7d37-c775-5b7b-b349-eb9dee4a1453" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434258 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186434256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434259 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186434257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434259 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bce2f3bf-424e-54b0-b537-ee61a51b4d2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186434259 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186434255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186