86045417] [17592186544609 #edb/ref 1080 "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544609 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544609 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f115935a-361e-5a7a-a92c-8717bff55eaf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544619 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544619 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544619 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f50dc0d2-5565-5274-afe9-0e9e574999f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544627 #edb/ref 1080 "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544627 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544627 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f6d9ca68-4ca0-505d-ba43-841000fa1d32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544715 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186544257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544715 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186544318 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544715 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186544390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544715 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186544396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544715 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186544529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544715 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544715 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544715 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186544396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544715 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "878eab3b-0013-5886-bc3a-c5e6e24549e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544808 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186544715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544808 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140954" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544808 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544808 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}5\\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ what is the second column of $U?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544808 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3d35be6f-b8bf-5aae-b526-fffd6ac155d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186544808 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that if $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ and ${\\sigma }_{i}\\ne 0,$ then the $i$th column of $U$ can be found as\n\n$$\n{u}_{i}=\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{i}}A{v}_{i},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${u}_{i}$ and ${v}_{i}$ are the $i$th columns of the orthogonal matrices $U$ and $V,$ respectively.  \n\nFrom the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that the singular values are ${\\sigma }_{1}=5\\sqrt{2}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the first column of $U$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{10} \\\\ \\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, we can't use the same formula to find the second column of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find a vector\n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nsuch that \n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,‖{u}_{2}‖=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nSolving ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{1}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{2}=0,\n$$\n\nwe get a nonzero solution $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Normalizing this vector, we finally obtain the  second column of $U:$\n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
